<MorpheusModel version="4">
    <Description>
        <Title>Anlas 2024: spontaneous AP patterning of an explicit growing cell aggregate</Title>
        <Details>Biologically grounded approximation of Anlas et al., Development 151, dev202171 (2024), DOI 10.1242/dev.202171. The paper is experimental and supplies no computational source model or fitted kinetics. This is a 2D Cellular Potts + cell signaling hypothesis, not an exact published model. Simulation time is hours post aggregation (hpa), lattice nodes are 2 micrometres, and 1 MCS is 0.01 h by default. All initial cells have exactly uniform Bra/T=0.05, Sox2=0.9, Wnt response=0.5, and cadherins. The initial circular Voronoi aggregate contains only the requested starting cells. No external axis, localized cue, prescribed future cells, spatial mask, or target snapshot is used. Isotropic stochastic signaling fluctuations generate symmetry breaking; the seed is for reproducibility only. Wnt/Nodal cooperation is approximated by Nodal-dependent bistable Wnt response with nearest-neighbor exchange. A population-mean Lefty-like inhibitor is an explicit untested fast-mixing approximation, motivated by T+ Lefty1 expression and the absence of a fixed pole length scale (pp. 7-9). T regulates Sox2 and cadherin state phenomenologically. Homophilic E/N-cadherin adhesion and CPM fluctuations support cell sorting and neighbor exchange (Figs. 1F,G and 5D). CHIR99021 stimulation is spatially uniform from 48 to 72 hpa, representing the reported 3 micromolar pulse; its response amplitude is uncalibrated. Cell cycle length 72 h is chosen to satisfy the requested 50-to-100-cell showcase, not a measured proliferation rate in the paper. Cells grow exponentially and divide physically, inheriting expression and resetting age and target area. Aldh1a2 and Eomes are qualitative local-response reporter hypotheses only; full lineage diversity, epithelial organization, 3D mechanics, and convergent extension are not reconstructed. All nonreported rates and energy scales are listed in evidence/source_audit.json.</Details>
    </Description>
